('<h2>3. Entonces, &#191;qu&#233; es redondear?</h2>', '<h2>3. So what does rounding mean?</h2>'),
('<p>Como bajar para siempre es imposible, en alg&#250;n momento hay que <strong>plantarse</strong> en un nivel. Redondear es justamente eso: elegir cu&#225;ntos decimales conservamos y quedarnos con la marca m&#225;s cercana. Veamos d&#243;nde cae 1/7 = 0.142857&#8230;</p>', '<p>Going down forever is impossible, so at some point you have to <strong>stop</strong> at one level. That is exactly what rounding is: choosing how many decimal places to keep and taking the closest mark. Let&#8217;s see where 1/7 = 0.142857&#8230; lands.</p>'),
